<title>FINLAND: Metra up sharply on dollar strength.</title>
<headline>Metra up sharply on dollar strength.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish engineering group Oy Metra Ab rose sharply on Wednesday on demand fuelled by the strong dollar, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1155/0855 GMT, Metra's B share traded at an all-time high 187.00 markka, up 9.00 markka or more than five percent. Metra's less-traded A share traded at 189.00 markka, up 10.00 markka or almost six percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Metra is one of the biggest beneficiaries of the strong dollar,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Trade in the B share was modest at over seven million markka. Volume in the A share was only half a million markka. @</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
